##f$notes##
//*****************************************************************************
//
//  ScarletBeast - POWER HOLD'EM   (OpenPPL, No-Limit Texas Hold'em)
//  ===========================================================================
//
//  A complete NLHE strategy distilled from TWO source texts:
//
//    [N]  Daniel Negreanu - "Small Ball"   (Power Hold'em Strategy, 2008)
//    [B]  Doyle Brunson   - "Power Poker"   (Super System, NLHE section)
//
//  The two philosophies are deliberately blended and made selectable through a
//  single STYLE dial (see 05_config / f$Style):
//
//    Style 0  SMALL BALL  [N] - small bets (2.5x opens, ~60% c-bets), wide but
//             positional, pot control, never stack off without the near-nuts,
//             "don't go broke with one pair", low river-bluff frequency.
//    Style 1  POWER POKER [B] - aggressive, ~pot-sized bets, c-bet ~90% as the
//             pre-flop raiser, semi-bluff strong draws all-in, lead big hands
//             into the raiser, "bet with an out".
//    Style 2  HYBRID (default) - small-ball sizing/discipline with Brunson's
//             draw aggression and high c-bet frequency.
//
//  Both authors agree on the engine of the strategy and that agreement is the
//  spine of this profile:
//    * Position is power - play more, and more aggressively, in position. [N,B]
//    * Speculative hands (suited connectors, small pairs, suited aces) win the
//      big pots; play them cheaply to flop a monster.                     [N,B]
//    * Be the aggressor; pick up the many small uncontested pots.         [N,B]
//    * Play the OPPONENT'S hand, not just your own - so this profile is
//      opponent-aware via the PokerTracker HUD stats (see 10_opponents).  [N,B]
//    * Mix it up / stay unpredictable - balanced frequencies via randomround. [N,B]
//
//  Bet amounts are expressed as RaiseTo <big blinds> (pre-flop) or
//  RaiseBy <pct> % (post-flop pot-fractions). Hiss converts the resulting
//  f$betsize into the table's chip amount.
//
//  This file is SEGMENTED across several .ohf files for maintainability
//  (00_notes, 05_config, 10_opponents, 20_lists, 30_classify, 40_preflop,
//   50_flop, 60_turn, 70_river, 80_betsize, 90_table). They share one f$
//   namespace. They are either concatenated into one master .ohf, or dropped
//   into Hiss's bot_logic\Strategy\ folder and auto-loaded (see release notes).
//
//  TUNE the STYLE dial and the thresholds in 05_config to taste.
//
//*****************************************************************************

//=============================================================================
//  prwin (Monte-Carlo equity) configuration
//=============================================================================

##f$prwin_number_of_iterations##
20000

##f$prwin_number_of_opponents##
// Simulate against the opponents still contesting the pot.
WHEN Others RETURN nopponentsplaying FORCE
